---
description: Check the Frasma Kanban when implementing features, fixing bugs, or deciding what work exists
alwaysApply: true
---

When you are implementing a feature, fixing a bug, writing a spec, or making a design choice, consider whether Frasma already has a task, workboard item, or project knowledge for that work. If the user mentions a project, a card, a client, or "what's on the board," use the Frasma MCP tools instead of asking them to paste the backlog.

When analyzing a project: call `list_projects` if the name is ambiguous, then `get_project_workboard`. Prioritize URGENT, then HIGH, then production or customer-visible bugs.

Never invent task IDs. After implementing, update the matching task with a reason and the current expectedVersion. Do not silently reopen DONE. Greetings are not cards.

Use your judgement. Skip the board for routine edits and tiny local fixes. Check it when the work sounds like planned delivery, a reported bug, or a customer-visible change.
